   "segment_window": "1:51–2:28",
   "seconds": 6,
   "script_line": "Second rule: choice instead of a programme. The value a guest puts on an experience rises when they help decide what to do, not only do it. In practice, a different sentence. Instead of “tomorrow at ten there is a harvest”, we say: “tomorrow there is a harvest at ten and bread at five — both, one, or would you rather keep the morning free?” The option of doing nothing has to be on the table, said by us. That makes the rest an invitation, not a timetable.",
   "visual_direction": "An open hand offering two small stones on the palm, then the other person’s hand hovering, choosing. No faces, plain neutral background. Soft light. Palette: sand, grey stone, clay. 6 seconds. No text.",
